{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Consistency Boundary.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Consistency Boundary.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"consistency boundary consistency boundary","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Consistency Boundary.md","fileName":"Consistency Boundary.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Consistency Boundary","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Aggregate Consistency and Persistence]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Aggregate Consistency and Persistence","Aggregate","Eventual Consistency","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Consistency Boundary.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Consistency Boundary.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"consistency boundary consistency boundary","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Consistency Boundary.md","fileName":"Consistency Boundary.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Consistency Boundary","heading":"Consistency Boundary","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A consistency boundary encloses the smallest set of state that must obey business rules immediately after an operation. Inside an [[Aggregate]], the root protects invariants across all child entities and value objects. State outside the boundary is not guaranteed to change atomically and may require messages or [[Eventual Consistency]]. Making this boundary explicit prevents a database-wide object graph from turning every update into a potentially conflicting transaction.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Aggregate Consistency and Persistence","Aggregate","Eventual Consistency","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Consistency Boundary.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Consis